/**
\page general_information General Information
 
 As briefly explained within the introduction the path tracking algorithm uses a local vcs-coordinate system grid array with a
constant granularity which is either placed on the longitudinal or lateral axis. This axis management is dependend of the path direction which
can be longitudinal backwards, longitudinal forward, lateral left or lateral right. For lateral paths the grid array, also called the grid component, 
is placed on the lateral axis (y-axis) while for longitudinal paths the grid component is displayed by the longitudinal component (x-axis).
When an object passes a grid point the position component, which is described by the lateral component for paths with longitudinal direction and 
longitudinal component for lateral paths, gets extrapolated with help of the current and previous object location. This is needed due to limitation of 
the sensors sample rate.

@image html flowchart.png "Flowchart of Path Tracking" width=1000px

Mainly it can be noted that the path tracking algorithm is separated into two modules. The first is the Path\_Track module in which the whole path management (e.g. creation, grouping and rotation) is done.
The second module is indicated by the Objects\_To\_Path\_Matching module. Here the best matching path is searched for the respective objects, also the output for other feature functions is prepared here.

 */